WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.333
SPEAKER 1: Welcome to this
episode of "Click to Deploy,"

00:00:02.333 --> 00:00:05.220
a series where we show you how
easy it is to deploy solutions

00:00:05.220 --> 00:00:07.200
from Google Cloud marketplace.

00:00:07.200 --> 00:00:09.060
In this episode,
we'll be reviewing

00:00:09.060 --> 00:00:12.300
how to set up a Confluent Cloud
cluster via the Google Cloud

00:00:12.300 --> 00:00:13.380
marketplace.

00:00:13.380 --> 00:00:16.530
Confluent is pioneering a
fundamentally new category

00:00:16.530 --> 00:00:20.310
of data infrastructure
focused on data in motion.

00:00:20.310 --> 00:00:23.370
Its cloud native offering
is the foundational platform

00:00:23.370 --> 00:00:25.560
for data in motion,
which is designed

00:00:25.560 --> 00:00:27.510
to be the intelligent
connective tissue

00:00:27.510 --> 00:00:30.900
to enable real-time data
from multiple sources,

00:00:30.900 --> 00:00:35.070
allowing it to constantly
stream across the organization.

00:00:35.070 --> 00:00:38.250
And, in fact, Confluent founders
are the original creators

00:00:38.250 --> 00:00:42.000
of Apache Kafka and are helping
organizations set their data

00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:45.240
in motion even faster with
their fully managed service

00:00:45.240 --> 00:00:46.980
for Apache Kafka.

00:00:46.980 --> 00:00:51.360
Now let's explore how to set
up a Confluent Cloud cluster.

00:00:51.360 --> 00:00:53.880
Let's start by searching for
Confluent Cloud in the Google

00:00:53.880 --> 00:00:55.410
Cloud marketplace.

00:00:55.410 --> 00:00:58.380
For this demo, we'll choose
the solution Apache Kafka

00:00:58.380 --> 00:00:59.970
on Confluent Cloud.

00:00:59.970 --> 00:01:03.510
The landing page will display
information about the solution,

00:01:03.510 --> 00:01:06.540
details about
pricing, and support.

00:01:06.540 --> 00:01:09.390
The pricing information
displays a high level estimate

00:01:09.390 --> 00:01:10.540
of charges.

00:01:10.540 --> 00:01:12.930
Pricing for this solution is
based on your subscription

00:01:12.930 --> 00:01:14.280
plan.

00:01:14.280 --> 00:01:18.580
Let's click the Subscribe
button to launch the solution.

00:01:18.580 --> 00:01:20.740
Start first by choosing
a billing account

00:01:20.740 --> 00:01:23.410
and agreeing to the
terms below, which

00:01:23.410 --> 00:01:26.170
are the terms about
subscription fee billed monthly

00:01:26.170 --> 00:01:28.130
and canceling the service.

00:01:28.130 --> 00:01:30.010
You'll also notice the
pricing calculator,

00:01:30.010 --> 00:01:32.560
which can help you see
estimated costs based

00:01:32.560 --> 00:01:35.530
on factors like time frame
and subscription plan.

00:01:38.950 --> 00:01:40.610
Once your purchase
has been accepted,

00:01:40.610 --> 00:01:43.030
you will see another page,
which requires you to register

00:01:43.030 --> 00:01:44.530
with Confluent Cloud.

00:01:44.530 --> 00:01:48.520
You'll be able to manage Apache
Kafka on Confluent Cloud.

00:01:48.520 --> 00:01:53.290
Make sure to sign in or log in
with your Confluent account.

00:01:53.290 --> 00:01:56.680
On Confluent Cloud, we
will set up a cluster.

00:01:56.680 --> 00:02:01.200
For the purpose of this demo,
I will create a basic cluster.

00:02:01.200 --> 00:02:02.760
Choose a region.

00:02:02.760 --> 00:02:06.870
We'll choose US 4, Las Vegas.

00:02:06.870 --> 00:02:08.220
Choose an availability.

00:02:08.220 --> 00:02:09.540
We'll choose single zone.

00:02:12.890 --> 00:02:14.255
Now we'll launch our cluster.

00:02:19.170 --> 00:02:22.500
Next, let's test for our
cluster using Confluent CLI

00:02:22.500 --> 00:02:23.790
on the Google Cloud shell.

00:02:23.790 --> 00:02:38.850
